00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.520
baseball, and wrestling.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.720
And when he had little girls,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.520
he hoped they'd have
his competitive spirit.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.390
And boy do they.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.520
It just happens to be
in a different sport.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.630
They're cheerleaders.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.707
And now he's happily
become a tried and true,

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:21.750
"Cheer Dad".

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.220
Even practicing the routines

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.123
with his girls like this.

00:00:25.123 --> 00:00:26.755
- Five, six, seven, eight.

00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:30.303
One, two, three, four, five, seven.

00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:32.136
One, go, three,

00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:33.553
five, seven, dip,

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:37.143
four, five, seven, and,

00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:39.127
one, two, three, five.

00:00:40.176 --> 00:00:41.771
(audience cheers)

00:00:41.771 --> 00:00:42.604
- Oh my gawd,

00:00:42.604 --> 00:00:43.437
I love your family.

00:00:43.437 --> 00:00:45.030
Okay, go Michael!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.170
We have him on the line right now

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.040
along with his daughters,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.570
Josie, who you saw in that video,

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.280
and her older sister, Anabelle.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.300
What's up everybody?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.153
How y'all doing?

00:00:52.153 --> 00:00:53.855
(audience cheers)

00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:55.060
- [Michael] Hey.
- [Josie and Anabelle] Hey.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:55.893
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:55.893 --> 00:00:56.760
So Michael, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.860
What's it like to be a cheer dad?

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.330
- Oh, it's awesome.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.193
So about three years ago,

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.670
Anabelle and Josie got involved

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.900
in All Star Cheerleading.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.860
And, ever since then I've
grown to love the sport.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.690
I taught myself how to teach them

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.523
how to do cheers

00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:12.240
and every day we'll go outside,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.350
we'll stunt in the front yard,

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.700
I'll help 'em with their tumbling.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.380
And it's really been a bonding experience

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.780
between all three of us.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.310
And, we've just grown
to love the cheer sport.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.690
- Oh, it's incredible.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:22.523
That's so cool.

00:01:22.523 --> 00:01:23.356
So Annabelle and Josie,

00:01:23.356 --> 00:01:24.750
how's your dad as a cheerleader?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.740
How do you think?

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.877
- He's getting better
every time I teach him.

00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:29.310
(audience laughs)
Because,

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:30.390
when we stunt in the yard

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.800
and work on our flexibility,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.563
and he's a great dad.

00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:34.396
- Aww,

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.263
I love that.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.230
What about you, Josie?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.730
